# Backend: .NET 10 + EF Core

Source: `docs/backend/dotnet-efcore.md`. Contract: `docs/api-contract.md`. Decisions: `docs/plans/backend-dotnet-efcore.md`.

- Never reuse Express + Mongoose code, templates or assets. Shared with Express: NormalizedModel, manifest, contract, admin config only.
- Decisions live in `dotnetContext.ts`; templates only loop over prepared lines. Paths / names only via `dotnetLayout.ts` / `dotnetModuleNames`.
- G files start with `// <auto-generated by Generator />` and `#nullable enable` on line 2; written through `writeGenerated` (skips header-less files). K files and assets through `writeOnce`; never overwrite.
- No custom blocks: user code goes in `partial` members in `*.Custom.cs` / `*Hooks.cs`. A G file must never require a K file to exist beyond what bootstrap / first generate creates.
- CRUD bodies only in `CrudServiceBase` (asset); module services override hooks of the base. One generic `ICrudService<…>` + per-module `partial interface`.
- Entity property lines keep the parser marker comment (`// <json> [unique] [trim] [required]`, `// nav`); change the parser and the round-trip gate together.
- Entities are never serialized; every response goes through `Projections.Row` (list / getOne) or `WriteRow` (create / update).
- Assets change only for new hosts (create-if-missing); note the change in the plan so existing hosts can copy it.
- Gates: `node scripts/verify/regen-dotnet.mjs` (build 0 warnings, idempotent, parser round trip, app flow, admin config), then `node scripts/verify/dotnet-e2e.mjs` (migration + smokes + Express parity; run in background).
